---
import { portfolioData } from '../data/portfolioData';
---

<section id="about" class="px-3.5 py-6 sm:px-6 sm:py-8 space-y-5 sm:space-y-6">
  <!-- Section Header -->
  <div class="flex flex-col sm:flex-row sm:items-baseline sm:justify-between gap-1 border-b border-[var(--edge)] pb-2.5 sm:pb-3">
    <h2 class="text-xl sm:text-3xl font-bold tracking-tight text-[var(--foreground)]">
      About Me
    </h2>
    <span class="font-mono text-xs text-[var(--muted-foreground)]">Philosophy & Craft</span>
  </div>

  <!-- Editorial Lead Quote / Hook (First Line: Distinct & High-Contrast) -->
  <div class="border-l-2 sm:border-l-[3px] border-[var(--foreground)] pl-3.5 sm:pl-4 py-0.5 my-1">
    <p class="text-[15px] sm:text-lg font-medium leading-snug sm:leading-relaxed text-[var(--foreground)] tracking-tight">
      I like turning ideas that exist only in my head into things people can actually use.
    </p>
  </div>

  <!-- Narrative Flow: Uniform Tone with Slightly Boosted Opacity for Optimal Comfort -->
  <div class="space-y-4 sm:space-y-4.5 text-sm sm:text-[15.5px] leading-relaxed sm:leading-[1.8] text-zinc-600 dark:text-zinc-300 font-sans">
    <p>
      I'm a 2nd-year Software Engineering student with a growing curiosity for everything that happens behind the screen.
    </p>

    <p>
      I started with frontend development because I loved the creative side of software: shaping interfaces, refining interactions, and making small details feel right. But the deeper I went, the more curious I became about what sits underneath it all: how applications work, how data moves, how databases scale, and how reliable systems are built.
    </p>

    <p>
      Now, I'm exploring the space between frontend, backend, and data engineering, learning how the pieces connect rather than treating them as separate worlds.
    </p>

    <!-- Closing Thought & Creed -->
    <div class="pt-2 sm:pt-3 space-y-1.5 sm:space-y-2">
      <p class="text-xs sm:text-sm text-zinc-500 dark:text-zinc-400 tracking-normal">
        I don't just want to write code that works.
      </p>
      <!-- Last Line: Distinct & High-Contrast -->
      <p class="text-sm sm:text-[17px] font-semibold text-[var(--foreground)] tracking-tight leading-relaxed">
        I want to understand why it works, build it properly, and keep getting better at it.
      </p>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>
